                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %p
              Here the only entry that needs further explanation is the one for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_{(2)}
              refers to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} 2-adic integers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}_{(2)}
                    \=
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_{n \geq 1} \mathbb{Z}/2^n \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is not
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-primary+group"} 2-primary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} 2-completion
              of abelian groups to finitely generated abelian groups as in theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalTheoremOfFinitelyGeneratedAbelianGroups"}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Adams+spectral+sequence#Convergence"} Adams spectral sequence – Convergence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋮
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\vdots
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    }
            %p
              as in the above figure. Namely by the above prescrption, this infinite sequence should encode an abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              such that it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              by itself of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \overset{p \cdot(-)}{\longrightarrow} A \longrightarrow \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
            %p
              (Because it is supposed to encode an extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              by the group corresponding to the result of chopping off the lowest dot, which however in this case does not change the figure.)
            %p
              Indeed, by
              %a{:href => "p-adic+integer#pAdicIntegersAspExtensionofFpByThemselves"} this lemma
              we have a short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    \\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}
                    \\overset{p \cdot (-)}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\to
                    0
                    \\,.
